meta {
  name: 34 Update Parameter Note
  type: http
  seq: 34
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/lab-reports/{{labReportId}}/parameter-note/{{resultParamId}}
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "content": "<p><strong>Sample was hemolysed</strong>, repeat advised.</p>"
  }
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
  test("returns the saved note for that parameter", function () {
    const d = res.getBody().data;
    expect(d).to.have.property("resultParamId");
    expect(d.content).to.be.a("string");
  });
}

docs {
  Save the technician's OWN text for ONE result parameter's Note on this report: the Notes icon beside Sync on
  Technician > Reporting > Patient Entry / Test Entry. `resultParamId` (a `LabTestResultParam.id`) is a required path
  segment and MUST be one of this report's own parameters (422 `VALIDATION_ERROR` otherwise; nothing is written).

  The parameter's CONFIGURED Note (Master Data > Add Test > Add Result > Notes, `LabTestResultParam.notes`, plain
  text) is only the DEFAULT. `GET /lab-reports/:id` returns it as `resultParams[].notes`. A parameter with no saved
  text of its own keeps showing and printing that default; once this endpoint has saved text for it, THAT text shows
  and prints for this report instead. This endpoint never changes the configured Note, so other reports of the same
  test are unaffected.

  Body: `content` - rich-text HTML from the Notes editor (required, may be an empty string). An empty string is stored
  as it is and means "no note on this report": the default does NOT come back. Capped like every note (1,000,000
  characters, 400 above that).

  **Cleaned on save.** The HTML is cleaned of anything active before it is stored: <script>, <style>, <iframe>,
  event-handler attributes (onerror=…), javascript:/data: links and CSS that loads a URL are removed; formatting
  (bold, lists, tables, colours, alignment, links, images) is kept. What the API returns is the cleaned text, and
  the length limit applies to it. The same rule covers every rich-text note (Master Data tests, Branch Lab Tests, the
  technician's per-report sections, Overall Result templates and results, the per-report parameter Note).

  Response: `{ "resultParamId": string, "content": string }`. The saved texts of a report come back as
  `parameterNotes: [{ resultParamId, content }]` on `GET /lab-reports/:id`; a parameter with no entry there has no
  text of its own.

  Printing: the row tag `{result_note}` (inside `{{#each results}}`; Latte `$row->result_note|noescape`) prints this
  text when the report has one, otherwise the configured Note. It is a rich-text tag: the technician's HTML prints as
  formatting, and the plain configured Note is escaped (and keeps its line breaks).

  Who and when: `LAB_EDIT_REPORT` permission; no technician setting gates it. Only while the report is Pending,
  Partial Pending or Saved: 409 `LAB_REPORT_PARAMETER_NOTE_NOT_EDITABLE` once it is Validation Pending or later (the
  same rule as the result values; Edit Report sends it back to Saved). The status is read again under the report
  lock, so a Submit that commits in between is not overwritten. The usual write locks apply too: 409
  `LAB_REPORT_LOCKED` if locked; a sent-out, cancelled-order or removed-test report is refused; 404
  `LAB_REPORT_NOT_FOUND` if missing/other-tenant/other-branch.

  When the test is sent back for a repeat the saved text is soft-deleted (`deleted_at` set, the row stays) and the
  configured Note shows again; the next save revives the row. Saving a note counts as work on the report, so a
  Pending report with a saved note is no longer "untouched" (it cannot be sent on without losing it).
}
